---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';

import {site} from '../config/site';
---
<Layout title="Privacy" description={`Your information deserves care. Read the ${site.shortName} demonstration website’s privacy.`}><PageIntro title="Your information deserves care." eyebrow="Privacy" items={[{name:'Privacy'}]}/><section class="section container" style="padding-top:0"><div class="rich-copy"><h2>A demonstration, with clear limits</h2><p>{site.shortName} is a fictional website concept. Do not submit sensitive health information, payment details, government identifiers or information about another person without their permission.</p><h2>What the forms collect</h2><p>Booking requests collect your contact details, care interests, provider and time preferences, and optional notes. Contact, support, newsletter and gift-card forms collect the fields displayed beside each input. Booking progress is stored in your browser’s session storage and is removed after a successful request.</p><h2>How information is handled</h2><p>When email delivery is configured, submitted information is sent to the practice inbox through Resend. Booking acknowledgments are also sent to the address supplied. In local demonstration mode, submissions appear in server logs instead of being emailed. The application does not write patient records to a database or filesystem.</p><h2>Cookies, maps & external services</h2><p>This site does not install advertising analytics. Local fonts and images are served from the site. Opening the map or visiting an external link connects to that provider, whose privacy practices apply. Essential browser storage supports the booking flow.</p><h2>Retention & requests</h2><p>A live operator must define retention periods, access controls and deletion processes before collecting real client data. Contact the practice using the contact page to ask about access, correction or deletion. Do not send identity documents through the public form.</p><h2>Children & updates</h2><p>The booking service is intended for adults aged 18 or older. This sample notice was reviewed on September 24, 2026. A real practice must replace it with a notice reflecting its actual services, vendors and jurisdiction.</p><p style="margin-top:2rem"><a href="/contact">Contact the team ↗</a></p></div></section></Layout>
